// Your tile proxy — the Cloudflare Worker that holds the MapTiler key. The app
// has no MapTiler key of its own; this is all it needs to reach MapTiler.
// Deploy it with `cd proxy && npx wrangler deploy`, then copy this file to
// Secrets.local.xcconfig (gitignored) and fill in both halves.
//
// Do NOT write these as one `https://host` line. xcconfig reads `//` as the
// start of a comment, so the value silently becomes `https:` and the app falls
// back to the demo basemap with no error anywhere. project.yml reassembles them.
//
// No trailing slash on the host: the app builds paths by concatenation.
//
// The Simulator shares your Mac's network. On a network that cannot reach
// *.workers.dev, run `npx wrangler dev` in proxy/ and set the scheme to `http`
// with the host `127.0.0.1:8787`. A real device needs the deployed URL.
TILE_PROXY_SCHEME = https
TILE_PROXY_HOST =

// Your Apple Developer team, needed to build onto a physical device: an empty
// team means simulator-only. Leave it empty if you have not got one yet.
//
// A free Personal Team is enough for your own iPhone, and Xcode creates it for
// you the first time you sign in — Settings → Accounts → Apple ID → Manage. Its
// ID is 10 characters, and the same Personal Team is reused for every free
// account on the machine. Two consequences worth knowing:
//
//   - Its provisioning profile expires after 7 days, so the app has to be
//     reinstalled weekly. A paid account gives a year.
//   - It is per-machine, so this is deliberately not committed: it lives in this
//     gitignored file and project.yml reads it as $(DEVELOPMENT_TEAM).
//
// A quick way to read the ID back if Xcode is being unhelpful:
//   defaults read com.apple.dt.Xcode IDEProvisioningTeams
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
